00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:08.160
more excited than afraid, that is not

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:10.280
irresponsibility. That's a trait, okay?

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.240
Safe decisions rarely create

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:14.920
extraordinary lives. All right, trait

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.640
seven is extreme ownership. So, this one

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:18.200
separates real entrepreneurs from the

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:20.280
people who just call themselves

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:22.080
entrepreneurs online, all right? When

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.440
something goes wrong and it will, I

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:27.080
promise you, what is your gut instinct?

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:29.240
Like, do you look for who to blame or do

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:31.920
you look in the mirror? Because extreme

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:34.800
ownership means the outcome is always on

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:37.160
you. The bad hire, the failed deal, the

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:40.760
missed opportunity, it's all yours,

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:42.680
okay? No excuses, no finger pointing, no

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:44.560
victim mentality, right? It sounds

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.600
brutal, but it's actually the most

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:49.080
freeing mindset that you can have.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:51.480
Because everything in your life is your

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:53.920
